					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/raptor6" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5169735); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5169735&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608645544" alt="raptor6" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5169735)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/raptor6" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5169735); return false;" >raptor6</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608644397 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Dec 2020 13:39</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-2845/comments/show">SCP-2845</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4850911">
									

<p>It was this time of year two years ago when the youtube algorithm randomly pushed me into learning about SCP, this was one of the articles that definitely helped push past my initial impression of &quot;Oh, so it's some /x-y, murder-monster fan-fic site&quot;. Two years and, I dunno, like hundred articles read and it's still one of my favorites. Coming back to re-read it to get in the winter solstice spirit.</p>
<p>That said, the one thing that bothers me about this is the frequency of the ritual. The castration? Sure, big deal. The baby-eating? Yeah, super disturbing, kinda forces you to head-canon clone use for it as a fresh supply of infants seems even less likely than infinite D-class resources. But both those things become comically unrealistic when looking at that time frame. Personally, I would've tweaked it so it only needed to happen once a year during the winter solstice/Saturnalia season. Even the Yule-Man takes the summers off.</p>
<p>But that's just me. I don't expect any changes, that would be ridiculous, it's just my personal opinion. Also, I really want to know what the &quot;hamfisted&quot; ending that everyone was complaining about in the beginning was&#8230;. I feel like I should know how to look at previous edits but I still can't figure it out and at this point I'm too embarrassed to ask</p>

							</div>

								
					
