<p>About the first point:</p>
<p>Since this SCP is designed to &quot;save humanity&quot; from sinful volks within before the corruption is too advanced, it would make sense for the book to simply &quot;force&quot; a challenger. If it is really a bad idea, I could work out some sort of &quot;punishment&quot; or &quot;bad thing&quot; that would happen if within a certain time span no person chooses out of their own free will to take part in the trial.</p>
<p>About the second point:</p>
<p>I really intend to make the tests as impactful and individual as possible. So there is an individual trial for each person with no reoccurring tests from past participants. I plan to make it a big emotional arc with character growth.</p>
<p>Now the price at the end is a bit&#8230;I say even a mystery to myself because originally I planned to make a reference to SCP 001 &quot;The Gate Guardian&quot; but I am not sure if I am allowed to do so since I am a newbie and with SCP 001 being a big deal to make references to.</p>

