<blockquote>
<p>several change machines would be purchased by the foundations and placed in various laundry mats and arcades where agents disguised as workers will place the half the non anomalous coins in the change machines and gather the money for funding</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm&#8230;not sure I follow this? Is the plan 'the foundation owns a bunch of change machines and uses them to convert the coins into notes' because uh,,,that's not how money works</p>
<p>Beyond this, my core issue is that 'the foundation tries to work out which coin is anomalous' feels&#8230;like it'd be really uninteresting as a follow up to the description since we already know that it's just, one coin being anomalous; but it also feels like the actual investigation might be just, really boring and a lot of repetitive 'we tested coins 1 through 100, none are anomalous' kinda things.</p>
<p>I feel like this needs a stronger central narrative that actually focusses on the like, coin duplicating and the Foundation using this for their benefit, and like, that going somewhere, whether it's like&#8230;just the Foundation gradually like destabilising the economy by printing money or like, the treasury department investigating them and trying to arrest folk for creating counterfeit currency or something.</p>

							</div>

								
					
