<p>hm. I kinda like the core of this: that the entity has this, collective intelligence and wish to better humanity, and it presenting increasingly extreme requests to the foundation who have to question how far they are willing to go to like&#8230;keep this thing satisfied.</p>
<p>My, concern is that it feels like it might be really hard to like, convey this conflict in an interesting manner: I guess really what I want to see is where the conflict goes and how the demands escalate? Like, to really get a feel for you having an idea of how you're going to pull this off.</p>
<p>The television show revival angle feels&#8230;like something that either needs to be the core conflict the article is built around or not included; having it as a minor thing would feel weird, I think. But I also think it'd feel&#8230;weirdly petty for the core so I'd probably not include it?</p>

