			<div class="content" id="post-content-4850780">
									

<blockquote>
<p>It's what happens after the SCP foundation gets a hold of Twist that makes up what this article is about.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay but like&#8230;you vaguely hint at Twist answering questions and being involved in experiments, and there being this big mystery around the LLUN aura and I'm left just asking one question: what's the narrative purpose of this all? Where does it go? How are you getting a reader invested in this LLUN aura thing?</p>
<p>My concern is that once Twist gets captured, the interesting chase stuff falls to the wayside and is replaced by a vague mystery around a complex aura that both powers and hinders a dude with no real stakes to the mystery. It also feels like all the time travelling and looping stuff that sets this up falls to the wayside and is replaced by the mystery of a person who can know everything but can't convey it, and I feel like reframing that to be the core and removing the whole Jack angle might make this stronger?</p>
<p>Iunno, it feels like I don't really have a good picture of what you want to do here yet.</p>

