				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608645544" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;" >cybersqyd</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608632840 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 Dec 2020 10:27</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13946225/a-photo-book-of-murderers">A Photo Book of Murderers</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4850765">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>There is an eighty percent chance that within the first hour if the person whose photo is removed their personality will stop being overwritten however for every hour it decreases by twenty percent. And for every hour less and less of the subject's sanity is retained.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This feels &#8230; really video game-y? Like just the way it works makes it feel like it's a cursed item from a game and not like, a thing which exists? I think because of the like&#8230;rigid, one size fits all progression which feels like it's kinda glossing over how everyone reacts to stuff differently and so it'd affect different people to different intensities and with different recovery times.</p>
<p>Beyond this, my core issue with this idea is that at it's core, it's &quot;thing what turns you insane&quot;, which is, generally not very interesting to me. The angle of tying this into the brutality of asylums isn't a bad idea here but it feels underutilised: it feels, almost more like something your pointing at to say 'wow isn't this horrifying' than like, something actually in the story that you're grappling with and showing the horror of?</p>
<p>It also feels like it doesn't go anywhere: there's no real arc or growth through this, so like, you might highlight the malpractice but you're not really telling a story with it so much as showing some material that is shocking? And it feels like this needs e.g. a single character or something progressing through this that builds up to some kinda ending that grants closure?</p>
<p>I don't think this idea is dead in the water so much as it feels like it needs to take all the pieces you've assembled so far and then use them to do something, y'know?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

